                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "doki doki literature club is actually one of my favorite games ever. i went into it thinking it was just gonna be some basic anime dating game but i ended up getting way more attached to the characters than i expected. especially yuri. idk what it is about her but shes always been my favorite. her personality, the way she talks about books, and how shy she is just make her feel different from everyone else.\n\nthe game honestly hit harder than i thought it would. i never expected a game like this to stick with me for so long, but even after finishing it i kept thinking about it. yuri's character really stayed in my head and made me want to replay the game just to experience everything again.\n\nthe atmosphere, the music, the characters, everything about this game is memorable. i wish i could play it for the first time again without knowing anything about it.\n\n10/10 game. yuri will always be best girl.",
